{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00007",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 0.93,
      "end_seconds": 3.99,
      "duration_seconds": 3.06,
      "text": "So, good afternoon. Have a seat and we'll begin."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 4.6,
      "end_seconds": 5.3,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Morning."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 6.51,
      "end_seconds": 11.39,
      "duration_seconds": 4.88,
      "text": "Good morning, uh, doctor. I came along to help out."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 12.1,
      "end_seconds": 16.92,
      "duration_seconds": 4.82,
      "text": "Good, that'll be useful. Pull up a chair. Alright, what brings you in today?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 17.88,
      "end_seconds": 24.2,
      "duration_seconds": 6.32,
      "text": "It's cramping pain in the lower tummy, doctor. She didn't want to come, but I insisted."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 25.05,
      "end_seconds": 27.18,
      "duration_seconds": 2.13,
      "text": "When did you first notice it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 28.32,
      "end_seconds": 34.79,
      "duration_seconds": 6.47,
      "text": "About... well, two years. I told myself I'd wait and see, and here I am."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 36.08,
      "end_seconds": 43.13,
      "duration_seconds": 7.05,
      "text": "Tell me a bit more about it: how bad it gets, how often, and whether anything makes it better or worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 43.53,
      "end_seconds": 53.16,
      "duration_seconds": 9.63,
      "text": "I'd say severe. It just comes and goes. Yes, certain foods. That makes it worse. I didn't want to make a fuss, you know."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 58.19,
      "end_seconds": 60.45,
      "duration_seconds": 2.26,
      "text": "Does it come along with anything else?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 61.21,
      "end_seconds": 71.01,
      "duration_seconds": 9.8,
      "text": "A feeling of not emptying fully goes along with it, most of the time. I mean, I've also been passing a lot of wind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 71.97,
      "end_seconds": 74.47,
      "duration_seconds": 2.5,
      "text": "How bad is it, would you say?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 74.98,
      "end_seconds": 78.28,
      "duration_seconds": 3.3,
      "text": "Well, about a five out of ten."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 78.54,
      "end_seconds": 85.67,
      "duration_seconds": 7.13,
      "text": "Okay, I'm following. Let me check a few things. Any weight loss, family history of bowel cancer or blood in the stool?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 86.25,
      "end_seconds": 89.2,
      "duration_seconds": 2.95,
      "text": "No, none of that at all."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 89.85,
      "end_seconds": 91.59,
      "duration_seconds": 1.74,
      "text": "Any anaemia or night-time diarrhoea?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 92.9,
      "end_seconds": 94.82,
      "duration_seconds": 1.92,
      "text": "Nothing like that, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 96.21,
      "end_seconds": 96.91,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Any fever?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 98.49,
      "end_seconds": 101.04,
      "duration_seconds": 2.55,
      "text": "Not at all, no fever."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 102.3,
      "end_seconds": 107.56,
      "duration_seconds": 5.26,
      "text": "Actually, um, doctor, I did notice fever. She doesn't always say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 107.91,
      "end_seconds": 112.91,
      "duration_seconds": 5.0,
      "text": "No, I don't think I did. Maybe a little, I'm not sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 116.59,
      "end_seconds": 123.65,
      "duration_seconds": 7.06,
      "text": "Alright, I'll note both what you've said and what you've noticed. How about your heart, any problems like that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 124.89,
      "end_seconds": 127.59,
      "duration_seconds": 2.7,
      "text": "No, you know, that's been fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 128.3,
      "end_seconds": 130.41,
      "duration_seconds": 2.11,
      "text": "And your skin, any changes there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 131.5,
      "end_seconds": 134.59,
      "duration_seconds": 3.09,
      "text": "No, you know, skin's been fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 135.84,
      "end_seconds": 147.84,
      "duration_seconds": 12.0,
      "text": "It's quite normal to feel unsure at this point. People often expect an instant answer, but a good assessment usually has a few stages, and today is mainly about narrowing things down and making a sensible plan together."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 149.19,
      "end_seconds": 151.75,
      "duration_seconds": 2.56,
      "text": "Well, that's reassuring to hear."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 152.99,
      "end_seconds": 158.77,
      "duration_seconds": 5.78,
      "text": "Okay, so the vitals from earlier. Pulse 74, temperature is 37.0 degrees, blood pressure 119 over 78."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 159.42,
      "end_seconds": 160.54,
      "duration_seconds": 1.12,
      "text": "Good, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 161.74,
      "end_seconds": 164.33,
      "duration_seconds": 2.59,
      "text": "One moment, the system's being slow today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 165.0,
      "end_seconds": 165.9,
      "duration_seconds": 0.9,
      "text": "That's alright."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 173.19,
      "end_seconds": 177.2,
      "duration_seconds": 4.01,
      "text": "Alright, I've got it. What medicines do you take regularly?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 181.26,
      "end_seconds": 185.03,
      "duration_seconds": 3.77,
      "text": "Oh, it's omeprazole, 20 milligrams, once a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 185.51,
      "end_seconds": 194.55,
      "duration_seconds": 9.04,
      "text": "Doctor, I think the last prescription for the omeprazole was 40 milligrams. We changed it at the last visit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 195.71,
      "end_seconds": 198.03,
      "duration_seconds": 2.32,
      "text": "Alright. Did you bring the up-to-date prescription?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 199.38,
      "end_seconds": 211.48,
      "duration_seconds": 12.1,
      "text": "Um, um, I don't think I have it with me. It's Colospa, when it cramps. I'm hoping you can tell me something definite."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 212.23,
      "end_seconds": 214.48,
      "duration_seconds": 2.25,
      "text": "Is the room warm enough for you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 215.78,
      "end_seconds": 218.84,
      "duration_seconds": 3.06,
      "text": "It's perfect, um, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 219.69,
      "end_seconds": 220.39,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Any smoking?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 220.71,
      "end_seconds": 224.68,
      "duration_seconds": 3.97,
      "text": "I used to smoke but I quit five years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 225.58,
      "end_seconds": 228.81,
      "duration_seconds": 3.23,
      "text": "What about allergies, to medicines or foods or anything else?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 230.31,
      "end_seconds": 236.99,
      "duration_seconds": 6.68,
      "text": "Yes, aspirin. I get a rash. Right, I'm allergic to shellfish, I get hives."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 238.4,
      "end_seconds": 242.9,
      "duration_seconds": 4.5,
      "text": "Is there anyone at home who can help you out if you need it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 243.7,
      "end_seconds": 254.4,
      "duration_seconds": 10.7,
      "text": "Yes, there's family around most evenings, and they've been very good about checking in, although they do worry more than they need to."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 256.0,
      "end_seconds": 261.96,
      "duration_seconds": 5.96,
      "text": "Any long-term health problems I should know about? I ask because it helps me narrow things down."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 263.0,
      "end_seconds": 275.27,
      "duration_seconds": 12.27,
      "text": "Hmm, I have anxiety, for nearly five years. I took the morning off to come in today. I looked a few things up online, and that probably didn't help."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 276.85,
      "end_seconds": 277.85,
      "duration_seconds": 1.0,
      "text": "Okay. Anything else?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 279.16,
      "end_seconds": 287.41,
      "duration_seconds": 8.25,
      "text": "Right, I've had acid reflux for about ten years now. It's the not knowing that gets to me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 288.87,
      "end_seconds": 298.94,
      "duration_seconds": 10.07,
      "text": "Okay, I'm following. Yes, I can see the anxiety in your file as well. Okay, acid reflux, that's already on your record. Good to know."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 301.78,
      "end_seconds": 304.69,
      "duration_seconds": 2.91,
      "text": "Let me have a look at you now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 306.27,
      "end_seconds": 307.75,
      "duration_seconds": 1.48,
      "text": "Okay, go ahead."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 308.57,
      "end_seconds": 311.7,
      "duration_seconds": 3.13,
      "text": "A little pressure here, tell me if it's tender."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 329.67,
      "end_seconds": 334.23,
      "duration_seconds": 4.56,
      "text": "Soft tummy, a bit tender on the left lower side, no masses."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 340.07,
      "end_seconds": 358.19,
      "duration_seconds": 18.12,
      "text": "All done, thank you, please sit down. Putting it all together, my working impression is irritable bowel syndrome as a working diagnosis. Coeliac disease is also on my list. Let me just recap so I've got it right. You've had cramping pain in the lower tummy for two years, severe, and no blood in the stool."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 359.49,
      "end_seconds": 361.91,
      "duration_seconds": 2.42,
      "text": "Yes, um, that's right."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 362.77,
      "end_seconds": 371.23,
      "duration_seconds": 8.46,
      "text": "I'm going to order a stool calprotectin, for bowel symptoms. That will help us see what's going on underneath and decide the next step."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 372.58,
      "end_seconds": 374.03,
      "duration_seconds": 1.45,
      "text": "Okay, that's fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0058",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 374.78,
      "end_seconds": 401.0,
      "duration_seconds": 26.22,
      "text": "Let's get a coeliac test, for bloating. I'd rather check than guess, and this is the quickest way to know more. Let's get blood tests, for bowel symptoms. I'd rather check than guess, and this is the quickest way to know more. Note down what you ate before the bad days, it often reveals a pattern. A short walk every day, even twenty minutes, will help more than you'd think."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0059",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 401.52,
      "end_seconds": 407.83,
      "duration_seconds": 6.31,
      "text": "And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0060",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 408.25,
      "end_seconds": 409.66,
      "duration_seconds": 1.41,
      "text": "Okay, I will."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0061",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 410.86,
      "end_seconds": 416.85,
      "duration_seconds": 5.99,
      "text": "I want you to come back or go to emergency straight away if the symptoms get worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0062",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 418.41,
      "end_seconds": 420.4,
      "duration_seconds": 1.99,
      "text": "Yes, I'll do that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0063",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 421.2,
      "end_seconds": 424.03,
      "duration_seconds": 2.83,
      "text": "I'd like to see you again in six weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0064",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 427.37,
      "end_seconds": 428.07,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Alright."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0065",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 428.89,
      "end_seconds": 434.69,
      "duration_seconds": 5.8,
      "text": "Tell me what you've taken from all that, so I can fill in any gaps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0066",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 435.56,
      "end_seconds": 439.93,
      "duration_seconds": 4.37,
      "text": "So, I come back in six weeks. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0067",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 441.46,
      "end_seconds": 446.08,
      "duration_seconds": 4.62,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. So, that's everything on my side. Anything you're unsure about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0068",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 447.32,
      "end_seconds": 449.09,
      "duration_seconds": 1.77,
      "text": "No questions. Thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0069",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 450.57,
      "end_seconds": 451.39,
      "duration_seconds": 0.82,
      "text": "Alright, goodbye."
    }
  ]
}